Build succeeded. Here's what changed:

**MSTest v4 fix:** Replace `[ExpectedException(typeof(T))]` with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()` inside the test body.

```csharp
// Before (MSTest v3)
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void MyTest() { DoSomething(); }

// After (MSTest v4)
[TestMethod]
public void MyTest()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => DoSomething());
}
```

This is preferred because it pinpoints exactly which call should throw, and you can also inspect the returned exception object for further assertions (e.g., checking the message). For async methods, use `Assert.ThrowsExactlyAsync<T>()`.
